    "https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3772": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Fine Arts (Painting)",
      "description": "Trinity College | Assistant Professor of Fine Arts (Painting) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Fine Arts (Painting) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit the following: Cover letter that summarizes qualifications and creative/research interests, CV, statement of teaching philosophy, two sample syllabi of courses taught (combined into one pdf document), 15-20 images of current work (images should emphasize breadth of work with limited detail shots) and 15 images of student work from classes taught (labelled and combined into one pdf document), and contact information for three references willing to provide letters of recommendation. Please note: maximum file size for each upload is 9 MB. References will be contacted for those finalists reaching interview stage of search. Please note: maximum file size for each upload is 9 MB. Review of applications will begin on November 15 and continue until position is filled. Please direct any questions to Lynn Sullivan, Search Committee Co-Chair ( lynn.sullivan@trincoll.edu ). Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Fine Arts (Painting) Tenure Track or Non Tenure Track Tenure Track Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Open Date 07/30/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Full or Part Time Full Time Position Summary The Studio Arts Program at Trinity College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning fall 2027 in the area of painting. The candidate will be head of the painting area, teaching across all levels of painting, overseeing facilities, and developing the curriculum in innovative ways. Other responsibilities include mentoring students, departmental service, participation and contribution to departmental programming, and service to the college. The teaching load is 2/2 for the ﬁrst two years (and 3/2 thereafter, ﬁve courses per year), with a one-semester paid leave every fourth year. Position offers a competitive salary and benefits, a start-up expense fund, ongoing annual research funds, conference travel funds and a personal studio space. We are especially interested in candidates who welcome the interchange of ideas that working at a liberal arts college provides, and whose scholarly and creative interests would lend to trans-disciplinary collaboration (whether via research or pedagogy). Additionally, we seek a colleague who will engage with the city of Hartford and is able to incorporate into their teaching the diverse roles of art in a global and urban context. Trinity is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. Qualifications Applicants must demonstrate evidence of excellence in teaching as well as continued, strong, professional accomplishments in their field on a national and international level. We encourage candidates versed in the history, theory, and criticism of contemporary art. The department prioritizes a candidate’s broad intellectual rigor and capacity to teach a wide spectrum of painting techniques and concepts to majors and non-majors. Applicants must hold an MFA degree or equivalent. Two years or more teaching experience preferred. Compensation Competitive salary and benefits, plus start-up expense fund. Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit the following: Cover letter that summarizes qualifications and creative/research interests, CV, statement of teaching philosophy, two sample syllabi of courses taught (combined into one pdf document), 15-20 images of current work (images should emphasize breadth of work with limited detail shots) and 15 images of student work from classes taught (labelled and combined into one pdf document), and contact information for three references willing to provide letters of recommendation. Please note: maximum file size for each upload is 9 MB. References will be contacted for those finalists reaching interview stage of search. Please note: maximum file size for each upload is 9 MB. Review of applications will begin on November 15 and continue until position is filled. Please direct any questions to Lynn Sullivan, Search Committee Co-Chair ( lynn.sullivan@trincoll.edu ). Posting Number F00297 Quick Link https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3762 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Sample syllabi Statement of Teaching Philosophy Additional Applicant Documents Optional Documents 300 Summit Street, Hartford CT 06106 | 860-297-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3771": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biomedical Engineering",
      "description": "Trinity College | Assistant Professor of Biomedical Engineering Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Biomedical Engineering Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To ensure full consideration please submit a cover letter that includes a teaching statement and a statement of research interests (both of which address your potential to supervise undergraduates from all backgrounds), a CV, your undergraduate and graduate transcripts, representative research papers, and course syllabi and evaluations (if available) as well as contact information for three people who will provide letters of reference. Applications can be submitted to https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/ with the review beginning on November 15, 2026, and continuing until filled. Please direct any questions to the department chair, Dr. Clayton Byers ( clayton.byers@trincoll.edu ). Trinity College is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Biomedical Engineering Tenure Track or Non Tenure Track Tenure Track Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Open Date 09/14/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Full or Part Time Full Time Position Summary The Department of Engineering at Trinity College, Hartford, Connecticut invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor position with a start date of July 1, 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong interest and commitment to undergraduate teaching excellence, develop a vibrant research program that integrates and cultivates talented undergraduate student researchers, and contribute to the institution and the profession through service. Qualifications A Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering or a closely related engineering field is required for consideration. We invite applications from candidates with broad research interests in biomedical engineering, but those with expertise aligning with Bioinstrumentation, Biomechanics, Device Design, Bio-Imaging, and Medical Robotics are particularly encouraged to apply. These areas are critical for new medical innovations including smart wearable and implantable health monitoring devices, high precision surgical micro-tools, and advanced imaging systems, to name a few examples. The abundant Biomedical and healthcare facilities in the greater Hartford area provide excellent transdisciplinary research opportunities. Compensation Competitive salary and benefits, plus start-up expense fund. Special Instructions to Applicants To ensure full consideration please submit a cover letter that includes a teaching statement and a statement of research interests (both of which address your potential to supervise undergraduates from all backgrounds), a CV, your undergraduate and graduate transcripts, representative research papers, and course syllabi and evaluations (if available) as well as contact information for three people who will provide letters of reference. Applications can be submitted to https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/ with the review beginning on November 15, 2026, and continuing until filled. Please direct any questions to the department chair, Dr. Clayton Byers ( clayton.byers@trincoll.edu ). Trinity College is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. Posting Number F00300 Quick Link https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3770 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Representative research papers Research Statement Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Sample syllabi Teaching evaluations summaries Additional Applicant Documents 300 Summit Street, Hartford CT 06106 | 860-297-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3769": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology (Genetics)",
      "description": "Trinity College | Assistant Professor of Biology (Genetics) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Biology (Genetics) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please submit a cover letter, CV, a graduate transcript, a teaching statement that includes your approach to engaging a diverse student body, a research statement that addresses how undergraduates will be incorporated your scholarly work, three representative research papers, and names of three references (who will be contacted upon submission) to https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com . Review of applications will begin on Oct 8, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Inquiries may be addressed to the Dept. Chair, Dr. Hebe Guardiola-Diaz ( hebe.guardioladiaz@trincoll.edu ). Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Biology (Genetics) Tenure Track or Non Tenure Track Tenure Track Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Open Date 08/25/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Full or Part Time Full Time Position Summary The Biology Department at Trinity College (Hartford, CT) invites applications for a tenure track position at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin in fall 2027. We seek a broadly trained geneticist with a strong commitment to teaching a diverse student body and an active research program that incorporates undergraduate students. We welcome applicants across a broad range of subdisciplines including genomics, developmental, functional, and population genetics; as well as a wide range of organisms (e.g., Drosophila , Xenopus , S accharomyces , etc.). We also look to hire someone that engages with students and colleagues across a broad liberal arts environment. The teaching responsibilities include introductory biology, an intermediate-level course in genetics with a lab, and an advanced course in the candidate’s area of expertise (such as cancer, cell, or developmental biology). Other teaching duties include non-majors science courses or first-year seminars. The teaching load is four courses per year for the first two years and five courses per year thereafter, with labs counting as full courses. The College offers a competitive salary and benefits, start-up funds, a one semester research leave every four years, summer support for undergraduate researchers, and travel funds to professional meetings. Trinity is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. Qualifications Candidates should have a Ph.D. in biology or relevant field, post-doctoral and teaching experience. Compensation Competitive salary and benefits, plus start-up expense fund. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please submit a cover letter, CV, a graduate transcript, a teaching statement that includes your approach to engaging a diverse student body, a research statement that addresses how undergraduates will be incorporated your scholarly work, three representative research papers, and names of three references (who will be contacted upon submission) to https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com . Review of applications will begin on Oct 8, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Inquiries may be addressed to the Dept. Chair, Dr. Hebe Guardiola-Diaz ( hebe.guardioladiaz@trincoll.edu ). Posting Number F00299 Quick Link https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3768 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Representative research papers Research Statement Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents 300 Summit Street, Hartford CT 06106 | 860-297-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3766": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Language and Culture Studies (postcolonial Francophone Studies)",
      "description": "Trinity College | Assistant Professor of Language and Culture Studies (postcolonial Francophone Studies) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Language and Culture Studies (postcolonial Francophone Studies) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please submit a CV, cover letter, teaching statement focusing on the candidate’s inclusive pedagogy strategies, and scholarly writing sample (not to exceed 30 pages). Applicants will be asked to provide email addresses of three references. Once a completed dossier is submitted, emails will be generated to reference providers, directing them to submit letters to a unique URL. Applicants using Interfolio (or other dossier service) should provide the appropriate unique Interfolio email address for each reference letter writer. Review of materials will begin Thursday, October 8. For questions regarding this position please contact Professor Priscilla Meléndez, Chair of the Search Committee: priscilla.melendez@trincoll.edu Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Language and Culture Studies (postcolonial Francophone Studies) Tenure Track or Non Tenure Track Tenure Track Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Open Date 08/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Full or Part Time Full Time Position Summary Trinity College’s Department of Language and Culture Studies invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor with a specialization in postcolonial Francophone Studies, beginning July 1, 2027. The Department of Language and Culture Studies offers courses in nine different languages and is committed to innovation in pedagogy across all levels of our curriculum. We are seeking candidates with a record of excellence in scholarship and teaching and whose research centers on Caribbean, North African, and/or sub-Saharan African literature and culture, of any historical period. The successful candidate will be expected to expand our course offerings in postcolonial Francophone studies, teach courses at all levels of French language as well as generalist courses in francophone literatures, provide courses in English that support our African and/or Caribbean Studies programs on campus, and participate actively in the service of our department. Trinity is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching diverse undergraduate students in an interdisciplinary, liberal arts context. Qualifications The teaching load is typically 5 courses per year, but new hires teach a 2-2 load in their first two years. Applicants are expected to have native or near-native fluency in French and English. Knowledge of another language related to the candidate’s geographic focus is desirable (including but not limited to Arabic, Wolof, or Haitian Creole). A PhD in French and Francophone Studies is required by July 1, 2027 Compensation Competitive salary and benefits, plus start-up expense fund. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please submit a CV, cover letter, teaching statement focusing on the candidate’s inclusive pedagogy strategies, and scholarly writing sample (not to exceed 30 pages). Applicants will be asked to provide email addresses of three references. Once a completed dossier is submitted, emails will be generated to reference providers, directing them to submit letters to a unique URL . Applicants using Interfolio (or other dossier service) should provide the appropriate unique Interfolio email address for each reference letter writer. Review of materials will begin Thursday, October 8. For questions regarding this position please contact Professor Priscilla Meléndez, Chair of the Search Committee: priscilla.melendez@trincoll.edu Posting Number F00298 Quick Link https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3758 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Sample of Scholarly Writing Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents 300 Summit Street, Hartford CT 06106 | 860-297-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3761": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Public Policy and Law",
      "description": "Trinity College | Assistant Professor of Public Policy and Law Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Public Policy and Law Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To ensure full consideration please submit the following materials to https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com by October 9, 2026: a CV; a cover letter (describing research and teaching, including your approach to teaching undergraduates from all backgrounds); sample of scholarly writing; course syllabi; course evaluations; a graduate transcript; and contact information for at least three individuals who will provide letters of reference. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Public Policy and Law Tenure Track or Non Tenure Track Tenure Track Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Open Date 07/27/2026 Close Date 10/09/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Full or Part Time Full Time Position Summary The Trinity College Public Policy and Law Program seeks applications for a tenure-track assistant professor with a focus on health policy, broadly defined to include policy domains that shape health or health equity. Our unique interdisciplinary program unites policy analysis and legal studies to examine critical societal issues. We seek candidates with the interest and ability to teach advanced undergraduate courses in their area of research expertise, courses on health policy, and an introduction to US public policy. Trinity is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. The teaching load is 2/2 for the first two years (and 3/2 thereafter), with a one-semester research leave every fourth year. The successful candidate will be eligible for start-up funds, ongoing annual research funds, and funds toward conference travel. Qualifications Evidence of scholarly promise and teaching effectiveness is required. A Ph.D. in Public Policy, Sociology, Economics, Public Health, Health Policy, or a related field should be in hand by August 2027. Compensation Competitive salary and benefits, plus start-up expense fund. Special Instructions to Applicants To ensure full consideration please submit the following materials to https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com by October 9, 2026: a CV; a cover letter (describing research and teaching, including your approach to teaching undergraduates from all backgrounds); sample of scholarly writing; course syllabi; course evaluations; a graduate transcript; and contact information for at least three individuals who will provide letters of reference. Posting Number F00296 Quick Link https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3759 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Sample of Scholarly Writing Sample syllabi Teaching evaluations Optional Documents 300 Summit Street, Hartford CT 06106 | 860-297-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3757": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology (Developmental)",
      "description": "Trinity College | Assistant Professor of Psychology (Developmental) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Psychology (Developmental) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates should upload a cover letter; curriculum vitae; statement of teaching philosophy (including a statement of your approach to teaching students from diverse backgrounds); evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., teaching evaluations, formal observations) and sample syllabi, if available; a statement of research interests; 1-2 representative research papers; graduate transcript; and three letters of reference to: https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com . We will begin reviewing applications on October 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Inquiries may be addressed to: Laura.Holt@trincoll.edu , Search Committee Chairperson, Department of Psychology. Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Psychology (Developmental) Tenure Track or Non Tenure Track Tenure Track Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Open Date 06/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Full or Part Time Full Time Position Summary The Psychology Department at Trinity College seeks to fill a tenure-track position in Developmental Psychology, beginning in July 2027. The teaching load is four courses per year for the first two years and five courses per year thereafter. Annual responsibilities will include a core course in Developmental Psychology, its accompanying laboratory, and an advanced course in Developmental Psychology. Other potential courses include Introductory Psychology, statistics and methodology courses, first-year and senior seminars, and/or courses in the candidate’s area(s) of interest. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain a program of empirical research and to engage bright, motivated, and diverse psychology undergraduates in that research. Opportunities for community-engaged research and teaching, including the development of partnerships that support student learning and scholarship, are substantial. Trinity has an on-site childcare center (Trinity Community Childcare Center) that works closely with faculty in the Psychology Department; a robust partnership with the Hartford Magnet Trinity College Academy, a grades 6-12 interdistrict magnet school with an early college program; access to the Learning Corridor, a network of regional public schools serving students at the elementary, middle, and high school levels; and strong relationships with surrounding health organizations, including Hartford HealthCare, the Institute of Living, Connecticut Children’s Medical Center, and the University of Connecticut Health Center. Additional opportunities for community engagement and collaboration are available through Trinity’s Center for Hartford Engagement & Research ( CHER ), which supports programs such as the Community Learning Initiative, the Liberal Arts Action Lab, and the Public Humanities Collaborative. Trinity is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. Qualifications We are seeking a candidate with training in child development (infancy, early, or middle childhood) and with research experience in any area of study within Developmental Psychology. Applicants should have a Ph.D., or ABD , in Developmental Psychology, with experience teaching undergraduates preferred. Compensation Competitive salary and benefits, plus start-up expense fund. Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates should upload a cover letter; curriculum vitae; statement of teaching philosophy (including a statement of your approach to teaching students from diverse backgrounds); evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., teaching evaluations, formal observations) and sample syllabi, if available; a statement of research interests; 1-2 representative research papers; graduate transcript; and three letters of reference to: https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com . We will begin reviewing applications on October 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Inquiries may be addressed to: Laura.Holt@trincoll.edu , Search Committee Chairperson, Department of Psychology. Posting Number F00295 Quick Link https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3756 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Research Statement Representative research papers Transcripts Optional Documents Sample syllabi 300 Summit Street, Hartford CT 06106 | 860-297-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3755": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Educational Studies",
      "description": "Trinity College | Assistant Professor of Educational Studies Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Educational Studies Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit a cover letter, CV, statement of teaching philosophy (including your potential to teach and supervise undergraduates from all backgrounds), graduate school transcripts (official or unofficial), a sample syllabus, a writing sample, and contact information for three references. Applicants are asked to list contact information for reference providers, including email addresses. Once a completed dossier is submitted, automatic emails will be generated to each reference provider, directing each referee to a unique URL where the referee must upload a letter of recommendation. Applicants using Interfolio (or other dossier service) should provide the appropriate unique Interfolio email address for each reference letter writer. Review of applications will begin on October 1. Please direct any questions to Elise Castillo, Search Committee Chair: elise.castillo@trincoll.edu . Posting Details Position Information Title Assistant Professor of Educational Studies Tenure Track or Non Tenure Track Tenure Track Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Open Date 06/22/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Full or Part Time Full Time Position Summary The interdisciplinary Educational Studies Program at Trinity College, located in Hartford, Connecticut, seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Community-Based Education. The successful candidate will contribute to Trinity’s strengths of community-engaged learning and high-quality liberal arts education by teaching and researching in the area of community-based education, broadly defined. We seek a candidate who is able to support our program’s learning goals , including a commitment to educational equity and justice. We would also value a faculty member who has experience with philosophical, historical, geographical, participatory, quantitative, or other non-qualitative methodologies. In addition to teaching in their area of expertise, the candidate should have the ability to teach our core courses (including our introductory urban education course with participant-observation placements in nearby Hartford public schools) and contribute to Trinity’s Community Action Gateway for first-year students. The teaching load is 2/2 for the first two years (and 3/2 thereafter), with a one-semester leave every fourth year. The successful candidate will be eligible for start-up research funds and annual funds toward conference travel. Faculty have excellent opportunities to collaborate with Trinity’s Center for Hartford Engagement and Research and the Center for Urban and Global Studies , among others. Trinity is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. Qualifications Applicants should hold a doctorate in education or a related discipline before the position begins in August 2027. Compensation Competitive salary and benefits, plus start-up expense fund. Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit a cover letter, CV, statement of teaching philosophy (including your potential to teach and supervise undergraduates from all backgrounds), graduate school transcripts (official or unofficial), a sample syllabus, a writing sample, and contact information for three references. Applicants are asked to list contact information for reference providers, including email addresses. Once a completed dossier is submitted, automatic emails will be generated to each reference provider, directing each referee to a unique URL where the referee must upload a letter of recommendation. Applicants using Interfolio (or other dossier service) should provide the appropriate unique Interfolio email address for each reference letter writer. Review of applications will begin on October 1. Please direct any questions to Elise Castillo, Search Committee Chair: elise.castillo@trincoll.edu . Posting Number F00294 Quick Link https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3754 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Sample of Scholarly Writing Sample syllabi Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents 300 Summit Street, Hartford CT 06106 | 860-297-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3657": {
      "title": "K.W. Davis Endowed Professor of Economic Organizations and Innovation",
      "description": "Trinity College | K.W. Davis Endowed Professor of Economic Organizations and Innovation Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help K.W. Davis Endowed Professor of Economic Organizations and Innovation Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Completed applications, including cover letter, CV, letters of recommendation, teaching statement, a writing sample, and official summaries of teaching evaluations should be received for priority evaluation by October 15, 2025 to receive full consideration (but will continue until filled). Video interviews will be conducted in the second half of October. Contact: Edward.Stringham@trincoll.edu . Applicants are asked to list contact information for reference providers, including email addresses. Once a completed dossier is submitted, automatic emails will be generated to each reference provider, directing each referee to a unique URL where the referee must upload a letter of recommendation. Applicants using Interfolio (or other dossier service) should provide the appropriate unique Interfolio email address for each reference letter writer. Trinity is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. Posting Details Position Information Title K.W. Davis Endowed Professor of Economic Organizations and Innovation Tenure Track or Non Tenure Track Non Tenure Track Faculty Rank Open-rank Professor Open Date 08/28/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Full or Part Time Full Time Position Summary Trinity College seeks to hire the K.W. Davis Endowed Professor of Economic Organizations and Innovation beginning January 2026 or possibly later. We seek scholars who are committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching and research. The position is funded by the Shelby Cullom Davis Endowment for American Business and Economic Enterprise at Trinity College, which was created to foster understanding of, and promote the activity of entrepreneurship and the operation of a market economy. This is a non-tenured Named Professorship with an initial three year contract with eligibility for five year contracts afterwards. This type of position and the renewal process will be clearly specified in the appointment letter. If the initial appointment is not at the level of Full Professor, promotion is possible. Qualifications Ph.D. or equivalent. Ph.D. in Economics, Sociology, History, or related field, or equivalent terminal degree, such as J.D. Ideal candidates have experience with rigorous student centered pedagogy that develops transferable skills in composition, research, public speaking, and full and fair consideration of diverse viewpoints in the spirit of the liberal arts. A preference will be given to candidates with interdisciplinary interests. Candidates will teach four courses per year, and are eligible for a one-semester leave every fourth year. in the Formal Organizations program, based on their specific interests and area of disciplinary competence from a broad established curriculum. Sample courses include: Formal Organizations and Market Behavior, Entrepreneurship and Markets, Entrepreneurship and Society, Issues in Methodological Individualism, Exit Voice and Power in Organizations, Normative Analysis of Organizations, College, Sports Organizations, and Matching Markets. Compensation Competitive salary and benefits, plus start-up expense fund. Special Instructions to Applicants Completed applications, including cover letter, CV, letters of recommendation, teaching statement, a writing sample, and official summaries of teaching evaluations should be received for priority evaluation by October 15, 2025 to receive full consideration (but will continue until filled). Video interviews will be conducted in the second half of October. Contact: Edward.Stringham@trincoll.edu . Applicants are asked to list contact information for reference providers, including email addresses. Once a completed dossier is submitted, automatic emails will be generated to each reference provider, directing each referee to a unique URL where the referee must upload a letter of recommendation. Applicants using Interfolio (or other dossier service) should provide the appropriate unique Interfolio email address for each reference letter writer. Trinity is a highly selective, independent, nonsectarian liberal arts institution located in the capital city of Hartford, Connecticut. The college maintains a rigorous academic profile complemented by a vibrant co-curricular program. With more than 2,100 full-time undergraduate students, representing forty-three states and ninety-one countries, we consider our location in a culturally and socioeconomically diverse capital city to be among Trinity’s most distinctive assets; and we cultivate strong connections with our surrounding neighbors and with institutions and organizations throughout Hartford and the region. As a preeminent liberal arts college in an urban setting, Trinity College prepares students to be bold, independent thinkers who lead transformative lives. Posting Number F00287 Quick Link https://trincoll.peopleadmin.com/postings/3650 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Sample of Scholarly Writing Teaching evaluations summaries Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents 300 Summit Street, Hartford CT 06106 | 860-297-2000 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://trincore-ibvxjb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/107": {
      "title": "Head Men's & Women's Cross Country Coach",
      "description": "Department: Athletics Category: Athletics JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Hartford, CT, United States Trinity College, an NCAA Division III institution located in Hartford, Connecticut, is seeking an individual to serve as its Head Men’s and Women’s Cross Country Coach. The Head Coach will provide overall leadership and administration of the Cross Country programs, including setting strategic direction for all aspects of the program, recruitment and development of student-athletes, competitive success, budget management, fundraising, alumni engagement, staff supervision, and compliance with NCAA Division III, NESCAC, and Trinity College rules and regulations. The Head Coach is committed to fostering a culture of excellence that supports the academic, athletic, and holistic development of Trinity College student-athletes. Trinity College offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, wellness, dental and vision, retirement savings with employer match, flexible spending and health savings accounts, disability and life insurance; paid leave and other paid time off benefits; tuition benefits for employees and their dependents; and a variety of other employer-sponsored and voluntary fringe benefit programs. The anticipated annual base salary hiring range for this position is $63,400 to $80,800 per year, with final placement determined by experience, skills, qualifications, and internal equity considerations. Bachelor's Degree 3-5 years of experience Ability to develop and maintain strong relationships with student athletes, prospective students, other coaches, leadership, faculty, and staff Ability to work independently as well as within a team Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work well in fast-paced and stressful environments Ability to maintain professional code of ethics Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion Ability to respond effectively to sensitive inquiries or complaints Schedule and coordinate work and activities of others Strong communication skills (both oral and written) and skilled in making presentations Experience planning, implementing and managing programs Ability to manage social media posts for the team Interpersonal conflict management skills Primary Responsibilities – List up to eight major duties of the job Designs, prepares, and runs practice sessions and competition strategies in collaboration with coaching staff. Coaches student-athletes during practice, at home and away events, and tournaments. Cultivate and maintains strong relationships with student-athletes, prospective students, other coaches, leadership, faculty, and staff. Actively recruits student-athletes, including communications and networking with coaches, parents, alumni, and counselors. Adheres to all NCAA and NESCAC regulations. Performs administrative tasks related to scheduling, budgeting, fundraising, equipment and facilities management, and rules compliance. Mentors student-athletes through regular conversations regarding schedule, academic priorities, wellness, leadership, and time management. Participates in various committees on campus. Teaches physical education classes and assists with varsity game management is needed. Perform other related duties as assigned and based on departmental need."
    }
  },
